'''Runes''' are cosmetics that can be applied to items to give them particle effects upon use.

== Runic Mobs ==
'''Runes''' are obtained from Runic Mobs. Runic Mobs are normal SkyBlock [[Mob]]s, but with {{Green|4x}} higher {{Stat|Health}}, and deal double {{stat|damage}}. They have a {{color|dark_purple|purple}} name tag, and a much lower chance to spawn. 

* Mobs that can become Runic have a {{Green|0.5%}} chance of being so when they spawn in.
* They are guaranteed to drop a '''Rune.'''
* They have a {{Green|0.1%}} ({{Green|1}} in {{Yellow|1,000}}) chance to drop a {{Item|Runebook}}.
* They have a {{Green|1}} in {{Yellow|100,000-500,000}} chance to drop a {{Item|Periwinkle Dye}}, depending on their level.

All mobs can be Runic except [[Ender Dragon]], [[Crimson Isle#Minibosses|Crimson Isle Mini-bosses]], [[Slayer]] Boss/Miniboss, [[Dungeon Mobs|Dungeon Boss]] or [[Dungeon Mobs|Dungeon Boss Minion]].

Certain runes are also obtained from [[Slayer]] or as special rewards.

== Runic Pedestal ==
'''Runes''' can be fused on the [[Runic Pedestal]] found behind the {{NPCSprite|Blacksmith}} and owned by {{NPCSprite|Dusk}}.

Fusing two runes will have a chance of upgrading the rune to the next level, up to the maximum level of 3. Upon success or failure, the second rune is consumed. If this process does not succeed, the remaining rune will not gain a level. The chance of success can be seen in the Runic Pedestal while hovering over the apply trigger. Regardless of the outcome, the player will gain Runecrafting experience. More experience is awarded upon success.

Runes can be fused to [[:Category:Swords|Swords]], [[Bows]], [[Chestplate|Chestplates]], [[Boots]], [[Helmets]] and [[Axes]], depending on the type of rune. The player's Runecrafting level must be greater than or equal to that of the rune, or they won't be able to fuse it. This only applies when fusing runes to items; the player can still fuse runes whose level is above their Runecrafting level. Fusing runes onto items will also grant Runecrafting experience.

